        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: لاغر شدن",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "لاغر شدن (lâghar shodan) — \"to lose weight, to get thin\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "او با ورزش پنج کیلو لاغر شد. u bâ varzesh panj kilo lâghar shod. He lost five kilos through exercise."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "lâghar 'thin' + shodan 'to become'; present stem shav-. The opposite is châq shodan."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "lâghar is an everyday Persian word for thin, but EtymDB has no entry for it, and its origin is not settled. shodan, 'to become', is inherited."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
