          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "چاق شدن (châq shodan) — \"to put on weight\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "او در تعطیلات کمی چاق شد. u dar ta'tilât kami châq shod. He put on a bit of weight over the holidays."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "châq 'fat' + shodan. châq is blunt; topol 'chubby' is kinder."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "châq is often linked with a Turkic word, but EtymDB lists it without a source and its origin is not settled. shodan, 'to become', is inherited Persian."
            }
          ]
        },
