          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "رژیم گرفتن (rezhim gereftan) — \"to go on a diet\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "مادرم از اول ماه رژیم گرفته است. mâdaram az avval-e mâh rezhim gerefte ast. My mother has been on a diet since the start of the month."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "rezhim 'diet; regime' + gereftan 'to take'; present stem gir-."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "rezhim was borrowed from French régime, 'rule, order', which EtymDB traces to Latin regimen (EtymDB); Lewis & Short gloss regimen 'a guiding, a rule' (Lewis & Short). gereftan, 'to take', is inherited Persian."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
